<title>MEXICO: Mexico cenbank accepts in principle joining BIS.</title>
<headline>Mexico cenbank accepts in principle joining BIS.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's central bank said it had accepted in principle an invitation from the Bank for International Settlements (BIS) to become a member.</p>
<p>Banco de Mexico said in a statement Monday, released shortly after the Swiss-based bank made its invitation, that &quot;the board of Banco de Mexico has decided in principle to accept the BIS invitation&quot;.</p>
<p>A final decision would be taken by the board once the BIS explained the terms of the subscription for BIS shares which would be offered to the Mexican central bank, it added.</p>
<p>-- Michael Stott, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 7902</p>
</text>
